<h1 id="privacy-title" class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl">Privacy and cookies</h1>
<p class="mt-5 text-sm text-coal/75">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-13">13 November 2026</time></p>
<div class="work-content mt-8 text-lg leading-relaxed">
<p>I (Johan Gant) trade as Three Paw Forge, at 206 Dunminning Road, Glarryford, Northern Ireland. I’m responsible for the personal information described here (the data controller). You can contact me at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> about your information or this notice.</p>

<h2>Email enquiries and commissions</h2>
<p>When you email me, I receive your email address, any name you provide, your message and attachments. If we arrange a commission, I may also need contact, delivery and order details. I use this information to reply, discuss your requirements, fulfil agreed work and keep necessary business records. Providing enquiry information is voluntary, but I may be unable to reply or arrange work without the relevant details.</p>
<p>For general enquiries, my lawful basis is legitimate interests: responding to people who contact the workshop and managing that correspondence. Where records must be kept by law, I rely on legal obligation. Where necessary, I may retain relevant correspondence for the legitimate interest of establishing, exercising or defending legal claims.</p>
<p>I use Google’s Gmail service to receive, store and send email. Google processes the contents of messages and associated information as part of providing that service. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a>. I do not add people who enquire to a mailing list or use their messages for any kind of advertising or marketing.</p>

<h2>Website visits and traffic information</h2>
<p>This is a static website hosted on GitHub Pages and delivered through Cloudflare. These providers receive technical information such as your IP address, requested URLs, request times and browser or device information to deliver the site, protect it against abuse and diagnose faults. GitHub logs visitor IP addresses for security purposes.</p>
<p>Cloudflare’s collects traffic statistics to understand overall website traffic and security activity. Cloudflare also provides network-error reporting, which allows supported browsers to report connection failures. I do not use advertising pixels or add a separate visitor analytics script.</p>

<p>My lawful basis for website delivery, security, diagnostics and traffic analysis involving personal information is legitimate interests: operating a reliable, secure website and understanding how it is used. Read more in the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a> and <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2 id="google-maps">Google Maps</h2>
<p>The contact page includes a static map image loaded directly from Google. When your browser loads it, Google receives your IP address and technical request information, even if you do not click the map. The coordinates in the request identify the workshop, not your device’s location. This site does not request access to your device’s location.</p>
<p>My lawful basis for including the map is legitimate interests: helping visitors find the workshop. Google processes information it receives under its own privacy policy. Use of the Google Maps features and content is subject to the <a href="https://maps.google.com/help/terms_maps/">Google Maps End User Additional Terms of Service</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy policy</a>. Following the map link opens Google Maps, where Google’s own notices and settings apply.</p>

<h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
<p>The site’s own pages and gallery controls do not set application cookies or use local storage to remember you. I do not use advertising cookies so you don't get one of those really annoying cookie consent banners (yay!).</p>

<p>Cloudflare may use security cookies when it needs to check a visitor or protect the site. Depending on the protection applied, these can include <code>__cf_bm</code> for bot detection (which expires after 30 minutes of inactivity) and <code>cf_clearance</code> to remember a successful security check (for the configured challenge period). These are conditional security features, rather than cookies every visitor necessarily receives. See <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/">Cloudflare’s cookie reference</a> for their purposes and durations.</p>
<p>You can use your browser settings to inspect, block or delete cookies and block third-party resources. Blocking security cookies may affect access to the site; blocking Google resources may prevent the map image from loading. No big deal, though.</p>

<h2>Sharing and international processing</h2>
<p>The service providers described above receive information relevant to their services. If you commission work, I may also share necessary details with a delivery provider, professional adviser or authority where needed to fulfil the order, obtain advice or meet a legal obligation. I do not sell your personal information.</p>
<p>Google, GitHub and Cloudflare operate internationally, so information may be processed outside the UK, including in the United States. The applicable transfer arrangements depend on the provider and service; their privacy notices explain their use of adequacy arrangements and contractual safeguards. You can contact me for information about the arrangements applicable to your information.</p>

<h2>How long information is kept</h2>
<p>I delete enquiries that do not lead to a commission within 12 months of our last substantive correspondence. If an enquiry leads to a commission, I retain relevant correspondence with the customer records for as long as needed to fulfil the commission, meet applicable accounting or tax recordkeeping requirements and deal with any outstanding dispute or legal claim. These requirements, the completion of the work and any unresolved issue determine when those records can be deleted.</p>
<p>Technical logs and diagnostic information held by the website providers follow their service-specific retention arrangements. Their privacy notices provide further details. Information removed from active systems may remain in provider backups until those backups expire under the provider’s retention arrangements.</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>Depending on the circumstances, you can ask for access to your personal information, correction of inaccurate information, deletion, restriction of its use or transfer of information you provided. These rights have limits; for example, some records may need to be kept to meet a legal obligation or deal with a legal claim. I do not make solely automated decisions about you that have legal or similarly significant effects.</p>
<p><strong>Your right to object:</strong> you can object at any time, for reasons relating to your particular situation, to my use of your personal information based on legitimate interests. Contact <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> to object or exercise another right. I will normally respond within one month, subject to any lawful extension, and will explain if a request cannot be fulfilled.</p>

<h2>Questions and complaints</h2>
<p>Please contact me if you have a concern about how I handle your information so I can investigate and respond. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO), the UK data protection regulator, through <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">the ICO complaints service</a> or by calling <a href="tel:03031231113">0303 123 1113</a>.</p>
<p>I will update this notice when the way I handle information changes. The date above identifies the latest revision.</p>
